  {
   "slug": "tattoo-aftercare-the-first-two-weeks",
   "title": "Tattoo aftercare: the first two weeks, day by day",
   "date": "2026-10-14T10:00:00",
   "excerpt": "What to expect, what to do and what to leave alone while your new tattoo heals.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A tattoo is an open wound for the first few days, and how you treat it decides how it looks for the next forty years. Here is the routine we give every client, day by day. Your artist may adjust it for your skin, so always follow their instructions first.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Days one to three</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true,\"className\":\"in-steps\"} --><ol class=\"wp-block-list in-steps\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Leave the wrap on for as long as your artist tells you, usually a few hours.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Wash gently with lukewarm water and unscented soap. Pat dry with clean paper towel.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Apply a very thin layer of the balm we recommend. Thin means you can barely see it.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ol><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Days four to fourteen</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Expect flaking and itching. Do not scratch or pick.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Keep it out of baths, pools, the sea and the sun.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Wear loose, clean clothes over it.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Keep moisturising lightly, twice a day.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"in-note\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group in-note\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Some redness and swelling is normal at first. If it gets worse after day three, feels hot, or you feel unwell, see a doctor and let us know.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>After two weeks the surface has usually healed, but the skin underneath takes longer. Sunscreen on your tattoo, forever, is the best thing you can do for it.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "aftercare"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "tattoo-care",
    "healing"
   ],
   "featured_media": "aftercare",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Sam Pell",
     "content": "Printed this and stuck it on my bathroom mirror. Thank you.",
     "date": "2026-10-15T08:45:00",
     "email": "sam@example.com"
    }
   ]
