  {
   "slug": "piercing-aftercare-basics",
   "title": "Piercing aftercare basics: saline, patience and hands off",
   "date": "2026-10-07T10:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Healing times, cleaning and when to change your jewellery, from our piercing team.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Most piercing problems come from one of three things: touching it, twisting it, or changing the jewellery too soon. The good news is that all three are easy to avoid.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The routine</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true,\"className\":\"in-steps\"} --><ol class=\"wp-block-list in-steps\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Spray with sterile saline once or twice a day.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Let it dry, or pat with clean paper towel. No cotton buds, they snag.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Leave the jewellery alone. No twisting, no turning.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ol><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Typical healing times</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"in-prices\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-table in-prices\"><table><thead><tr><th>Piercing</th><th>Healing time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Earlobe</td><td>6 to 8 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Helix and other cartilage</td><td>6 to 12 months</td></tr><tr><td>Nostril</td><td>4 to 6 months</td></tr><tr><td>Eyebrow</td><td>2 to 3 months</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><!-- /wp:table --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"in-note\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group in-note\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Healing times vary from person to person. Come back for a free check-up and downsize after the first few weeks; swelling goes down and a shorter bar heals better.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If anything feels wrong, come and see us. Checks are always free, even years later.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "aftercare",
    "piercing"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "piercing-care",
    "healing"
   ],
   "featured_media": "piercing-tray",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "artist-spotlight-mara-vell",
   "title": "Artist spotlight: Mara Vell and the art of bold lines",
   "date": "2026-09-30T15:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Twelve years in, Mara still draws every design by hand. We talk roses, rules and why traditional work ages best.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Mara Vell has been tattooing for twelve years and drawing for as long as she can remember. Her work is traditional: bold black outlines, a small palette of solid colours, designs you can read from across the room.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>She draws every piece by hand on paper before it goes anywhere near skin, and keeps a stack of sketchbooks under the counter that clients are welcome to browse.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Bold will hold. Fine detail is beautiful on day one. Bold lines are beautiful on day ten thousand.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Mara Vell</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What she loves to tattoo</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Roses, in every possible arrangement</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Daggers and swords with banners</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Animals with a little bit of attitude</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Anything with a ship in it</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:gallery {\"columns\":3,\"linkTo\":\"none\",\"className\":\"in-flash\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-3 is-cropped in-flash\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:flash-dagger-rose}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:flash-dagger-rose}}\" alt=\"Flash design: a dagger through a red rose\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:flash-dagger-rose}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Rose</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:flash-snake}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:flash-snake}}\" alt=\"Flash design: a coiled green snake\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:flash-snake}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Snake</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:flash-anchor}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:flash-anchor}}\" alt=\"Flash design: an anchor wrapped in rope\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:flash-anchor}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Anchor</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --></figure><!-- /wp:gallery --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Mara books two months ahead and keeps one walk-in day a month. Follow the journal for dates.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "artists"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "traditional",
    "artists"
   ],
   "featured_media": "artist-mara",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Kit Moreau",
     "content": "Mara did my anchor. Six years on, still crisp.",
     "date": "2026-10-01T11:20:00",
     "email": "kit@example.com"
    }
   ]
