  {
   "slug": "artist-spotlight-jonah-reyes",
   "title": "Artist spotlight: Jonah Reyes, botanical fine line",
   "date": "2026-09-22T15:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Ferns, wildflowers and single-needle leaves: Jonah's quiet, detailed work and how he designs for the way skin ages.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Where Mara goes bold, Jonah goes delicate. His botanical work uses fine lines and soft shading, and he spends a long time on placement so a design moves with the body.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>He is also honest about the limits of fine line. Very small, very detailed tattoos can blur over the years, so he designs a little bigger and a little simpler than clients often ask for.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Before you book with Jonah</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Bring reference photos of the plants you love.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Be open to size changes; he will explain why.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Expect a consultation before the session.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:pullquote --><figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote\"><blockquote><p>I design for the tattoo you will have in twenty years, not just the one you will post tomorrow.</p></blockquote></figure><!-- /wp:pullquote --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Jonah's books open on the first Monday of every month.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "artists"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "fine-line",
    "artists"
   ],
   "featured_media": "artist-jonah",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "preparing-for-your-first-tattoo",
   "title": "Preparing for your first tattoo: a no-nonsense checklist",
   "date": "2026-09-15T10:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Sleep, food, clothes and questions to ask: everything to sort out before your first session.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>First tattoos are exciting and a little nerve-wracking, and that is completely normal. Most of the nerves go away once you know what to expect, so here is everything we wish every first-timer knew.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The day before</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true,\"className\":\"in-steps\"} --><ol class=\"wp-block-list in-steps\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Sleep properly. Tired skin and tired people both bleed more.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Skip alcohol for at least 24 hours.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Moisturise the area, but do not shave it; we will do that.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ol><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">On the day</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Eat a proper meal an hour or two before.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Wear comfortable clothes that give easy access to the area.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Bring water, a snack and something to listen to.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Bring photo ID.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"in-note\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group in-note\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>You can ask for a break at any time. Good artists expect it, and nobody will judge you.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Most of all, ask questions. About the design, the price, the aftercare, anything. A good studio is happy to answer every one.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "guides"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "first-tattoo",
    "tattoo-care"
   ],
   "featured_media": "studio-chair",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Lena Strom",
     "content": "The snack tip saved me during a four-hour session.",
     "date": "2026-09-16T14:00:00",
     "email": "lena@example.com"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "slug": "guest-artist-week-november",
   "title": "Guest artist week: Ottilie Brand joins us in November",
   "date": "2026-09-05T12:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Moons, moths and night skies: a guest artist from the north coast takes over the second chair for one week.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We are very happy to welcome Ottilie Brand for a week in November. Ottilie is known for dreamy night-sky work: moons with faces, moths, stars and quiet little constellations.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>She will be working from our second chair from the 17th to the 22nd, and has drawn a special flash sheet for the week.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Her flash sheet has eighteen designs, from a tiny crescent you could fit on a finger to a full moth with patterned wings for the back of a hand.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:flash-moon}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:flash-moon}}\" alt=\"Flash design: a crescent moon with a face and stars\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:flash-moon}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">One of the designs from Ottilie's flash sheet.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Booking</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Bookings open on the 1st of October through the booking page. Ottilie is taking deposits for custom work and keeping Saturday for walk-in flash.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "studio-news",
    "artists"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "events",
    "guest-artists"
   ],
   "featured_media": "flash-moon",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "covering-up-old-tattoos",
   "title": "Covering up old tattoos: what is possible and what is not",
   "date": "2026-08-28T10:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Darker, bigger and smarter: how a cover-up works, and how to know if yours is a good candidate.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Not every tattoo ages the way we hoped, and plenty of people come to us wanting to cover one up. It is often possible, but it helps to understand the basic rule: a cover-up needs to be darker and usually bigger than the original.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Good candidates</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Faded or blurred older work</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Small names or script</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Lightly coloured designs</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Harder cases</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Very dark, solid black areas</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Fresh tattoos that have not settled</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Designs on thin skin like wrists and fingers</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Sometimes a few sessions of laser lightening first makes a much better cover-up possible. We will always tell you honestly what we think, and we are happy to refer you if another artist would do it better.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"in-note\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group in-note\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Bring a clear photo of the old tattoo to your consultation, in daylight if possible.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group -->",
   "categories": [
    "guides"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "cover-ups"
   ],
   "featured_media": "flash-eye",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  }
 ],
